# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the TiwShirts static HTML website.

## Implementation Details

### 1. Fetched Latest Documentation
Retrieved the latest Vercel Web Analytics installation instructions from the official documentation:
https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

### 2. Framework Identification
Identified the project as a **static HTML website** (no framework like Next.js, React, etc.)

### 3. Package Installation
- Created `package.json` for project dependency management
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version 1.6.1)
- Generated `package-lock.json` for dependency locking

### 4. Analytics Integration
Added the Vercel Web Analytics script to **all 14 HTML files** in the project:

**Modified HTML Files:**
- ✓ index.html (main landing page)
- ✓ drop-01.html (products collection page)
- ✓ loja.html (store page)
- ✓ blog.html
- ✓ manifesto.html
- ✓ manualdousuario-cannabis.html
- ✓ politica.html
- ✓ sobre.html
- ✓ camiseta-just-doob-it.html
- ✓ camiseta-legaliza.html
- ✓ camiseta-maconha-salva-vidas.html
- ✓ camiseta-maconheiro.html
- ✓ camiseta-nao-somos-ma-pessoa.html
- ✓ view_images.html (utility page with UTF-16 encoding)

**Analytics Script Added:**
```html
<!-- Vercel Web Analytics -->
<script>
    window.va = window.va || function () { (window.vaq = window.vaq || []).push(arguments); };
</script>
<script defer src="/_vercel/insights/script.js"></script>
```

The script was inserted before the `</head>` tag in all pages (or before `</html>` for view_images.html which has minimal structure).

### 5. Additional Configuration
- Created `.gitignore` file to exclude `node_modules/` from version control
- Preserved existing code structure and formatting
- Handled special case of UTF-16 encoded file (view_images.html)

## Files Created/Modified

**Created:**
- `package.json` - Project configuration with @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Dependency lock file for consistent installs
- `.gitignore` - Git ignore file to exclude node_modules

**Modified:**
- All 14 HTML files with Vercel Analytics script integration

## Implementation Approach

Following the official Vercel documentation for static HTML sites, the implementation uses:
1. Inline script initialization that creates the `window.va` function
2. Deferred loading of the Vercel Insights script from `/_vercel/insights/script.js`

This approach ensures:
- ✓ No JavaScript errors if analytics fails to load
- ✓ Non-blocking page load (using `defer` attribute)
- ✓ Automatic tracking when deployed to Vercel
- ✓ Access to page views and Web Vitals metrics in Vercel dashboard

## Next Steps for Deployment

1. **Enable Analytics in Vercel Dashboard:**
   - Navigate to your project in Vercel dashboard
   - Go to Analytics section
   - Click "Enable" button

2. **Deploy to Vercel:**
   - The analytics will automatically start tracking after deployment
   - The `/_vercel/insights/*` routes will be available

3. **Verify Installation:**
   - After deployment, check browser Network tab
   - Look for successful requests to `/_vercel/insights/view`
   - Confirm page views appear in Vercel Analytics dashboard

## Technical Notes

- Used npm as the package manager (automatically detected)
- Handled mixed encodings (UTF-8 and UTF-16) across HTML files
- All existing functionality preserved
- No breaking changes introduced
- Analytics script loads asynchronously to avoid blocking page rendering
